Subject: Release owned GX default resources during shutdown

Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

The default texture bind group, sampler, texture/view, and pipeline layout kept
the Dawn device/adapter/instance alive until static destruction after SDL/video
shutdown. The validation-layer crash backtrace ends in the static bind-group
release. Release these references with the other GX layouts while the graphics
and window lifecycle is still active.

--- a/lib/gx/gx.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/gx.cpp
@@ -610,6 +610,11 @@
 
 void shutdown() noexcept {
   // TODO we should probably store this all in g_state.gx instead
+  g_emptyTextureBindGroup = {};
+  sEmptySampler = {};
+  sEmptyTextureView = {};
+  sEmptyTexture = {};
+  sPipelineLayout = {};
   sSamplerBindGroupLayout = {};
   sTextureBindGroupLayout = {};
   {
